.ie \n(.g .ds Aq \(aq
.el .ds Aq '
.TH batten-exec 1  batten 
.SH NAME
batten\-exec \- Run a command, passing its streams and its exit code through unchanged
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBbatten exec\fR [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] <\fIcommand\fR> 
.SH DESCRIPTION
Run a command, passing its streams and its exit code through unchanged
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help
.TP
<\fIcommand\fR>
The command to run, after `\-\-`, with its own arguments intact
